Changes in version 0.99.3 (2026-11-21):
* Add Bioconductor installation instructions to the README alongside the
  GitHub development installation, retaining the existing vignette instructions.
* Correct log messages for Tweedie index and heatmap plots, and remove redundant
  output arguments from internal plot helpers and their callers.
* Remove the unused full Franzosa MultiAssayExperiment RData file and its
  generation code. Retain the compact vignette example and its provenance.
* Condense and reorganize the README around supported inputs, a runnable
  example, and result interpretation, with detailed options in the vignette
  and function documentation.

Changes in version 0.99.2 (2026-11-20):
* Split .Tweedieverse_single() into a short function and explicit
  helpers for validation, input extraction, sample alignment, reference levels,
  filtering, variance-power resolution, offsets, formulas, fitting, result
  summaries, median comparison, prevalence tests, output files, and plots.
  Preserve the public interface and scoped logging cleanup.
* Apply styler and consistent four-space indentation to R code, tests, and
  preparation scripts. Wrap long code and documentation lines, normalize line
  endings, and preserve condition messages without paste calls in signals.
* Regenerate and format function documentation and record the current roxygen2
  version used for generation.
* Correct the motivation's spelling and model descriptions, remove the
  unsupported benchmark/power claim, and use the verified MaAsLin3 Bioconductor
  package link. Format the vignette's code and result-column explanations.
* Replace the SC2P-derived non-UMI data in both nonumi_sce.rds and the combined
  tweedieverse_data.RData bundle with original Tabula Muris Smart-seq2 brain
  counts and annotations explicitly licensed CC BY 4.0. Retain 20 genes and
  60 cells, balanced between astrocytes and oligodendrocytes from one mouse.
* Pin the replacement's original Figshare version, file identifiers, and MD5
  checksums. Include the source metadata record and attribution, and record the
  licence, protocol, source identifiers, and processing in the example object.
  Calculate SCRAN factors from all source genes before selecting bundled genes.
* Update the data preparation script, provenance and licence documentation,
  vignette source description, factor reference, and interpretation for the
  replacement dataset. Remove the superseded SC2P GPL-2 notice.
* Extend bundled-data tests to check the replacement's mouse, cell types,
  non-negative integer counts, source DOI, protocol, and explicit data licence.
* Remove SeuratObject from Suggests and document it as a separately installed
  prerequisite used only by the manual PBMC preparation script.
* Retain historical entropy-source attribution and move its full source URL
  into inst/COPYRIGHTS while keeping source lines within the width convention.
* Clarify that .gitignore excludes .DS_Store at every directory level and
  extend .Rbuildignore to exclude nested .DS_Store files. Verify that no such
  files are tracked and that docs/ remains excluded from package builds.

Changes in version 0.99.1 (2026-11-18):
* Keep zero-row MultiAssayExperiment result tables when a layer has no
  significant associations, preserving the other layers and output columns.
* Compare existing Bioconductor and CRAN modeling tools in the vignette and
  describe the workflow Tweedieverse adds.
* Expand the vignette with output-column explanations,
  worked interpretations, and an association heatmap.
  Update README examples to use defined containers.
* Provide individual RDS example files and load them explicitly with readRDS().
  Retain the combined RData bundle for compatibility.
* Replace the three toy containers with compact real-data subsets from the
  TweedieLabs source datasets: HMP2, PBMC3k, and SC2P brain data from GSE67835.
  Record preparation steps, source checksums, and dataset-specific licences.
* Document sources, processing, and per-object licences for the bundled data.
  Add a reconstruction script using pinned public source files and checksums.
  Remove redundant TSV files and the tracked .DS_Store, and
  exclude docs/ from package builds.
* Record Ali Rahnavard as a contributor and copyright holder and Himel Mallick
  as an author and copyright holder. Remove redundant contributor roles from
  authors.
* Replace the RPubs-derived entropy implementation with a direct calculation
  from Shannon's formula, preserving metadata-filtering and missing-value
  behavior. Retain historical source credit and remove unused information-gain
  helpers from the same source.
* Remove read_input_table() and obsolete feature/metadata file-input branches
  from internal association plotting.
* Credit MaAsLin 3 authors William Nickols and Jacob Nearing for adapted
  median-comparison simulation and covariance-adjustment code. Record its
  MIT license and retain the upstream copyright and permission notice.
* Move legacy-input validation into a seeded test and strengthen
  MultiAssayExperiment simulations to verify known effects and per-layer offsets.
* Rename the exported theme_omicsEye() helper to tweedie_theme() and update
  plotting functions and documentation.
* Rename the exported entropy() helper to tweedie_entropy() and update its
  internal callers and documentation. Clarify the default metadata filter.
* Restore logging handlers and levels after output-producing calls and after
  the MaAsLin2 backend, including when a call fails.
* Compute feature sample counts and zero proportions with column sums and
  match them to association rows by feature name.
* Remove obsolete commented-out code and inline entropy example comments.
* Validate link, base_model, correction, optimizer, and domain using match.arg(),
  so invalid optimizer errors list the optimizer choices.
* Report a failed feature fit once with its name and error reason, without
  retrying the identical fit.
* Add median_comparison_seed to Tweedieverse() and seed to
  median_comparison_tweedie(). Scope supplied simulation seeds with withr.
* Add return_all = TRUE to retrieve the full result table in memory, including
  with output = NULL and for individual MultiAssayExperiment layers.
* Align container assay columns directly with metadata row names and report
  informative errors for unmatched samples, missing effects, and missing assays.
* Preserve sparse assays through filtering and Tweedie fitting and pass sparse
  counts directly to scran. Remove obsolete table-input branches from the
  analysis path.
* Exclude missing q-values when selecting significant results after median
  comparison.
* Align MultiAssayExperiment sample metadata using sampleMap, including assay
  column names that differ from primary sample names.
* Clarify fixed-effect offset formulas by using + offset(log(offset)).
  R treats - offset(...) as equivalent to + offset(...), so the original
  fixed-effect models already included the offset.
* Preserve log size-factor offsets when adding random effects. The previous
  mixed-effect formula reconstruction dropped the offset.
* Add regression tests that verify offsets in fixed-effect and mixed-effect
  abundance models and compare adjust_offset = TRUE and FALSE.
* Add min_presence_absence_count, which defaults to three detected and three
  undetected samples per feature. Retained features below either minimum skip
  the prevalence fit.
* Use the abundance p-value directly when the prevalence p-value is missing.
  Combine an exact p-value pair of 0 and 1 as 0 in either order.
* Document these rules in the README and the bulk RNA-seq tutorial.

Changes in version 0.1.0 (2021-03-03):
* Initial tagged release.
